    "rationale": "* Small and wide-context: 4 layers x 256 dims (~3.2M params) is enough capacity for TinyStories'\n  ~1.5K-word vocabulary (Eldan & Li, 2023 show very small models already produce fluent stories), and\n  it trains 10 full epochs on a single T4 in roughly an hour.\n* Context of 256 characters (~50 words) lets attention see about two sentences, which is what a\n  character model needs to keep names and subjects consistent.\n* Weight tying reduces parameters and ties the input and output character representations together,\n  which usually lowers validation loss for small vocabularies.\n* lr 1e-3 with 500 warm-up steps and cosine decay: small models tolerate a high peak LR; warm-up\n  avoids early Adam instability, and cosine decay gives a low final LR for a good last checkpoint.\n* Dropout 0.1 because 100K stories x 10 epochs is enough data that heavy regularisation is not needed.\n"
